in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @smarts
in @frame
in @magic
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @smarts/frame — the cognitive-order-altitude adapter species.
# Bridges the @smarts family (substrate-architectural integration;
# #83) with the @frame family (cognitive-order substrate-decl; #82)
# honestly via the adapter pattern, following the @smarts/{pack,magic}
# precedents (ticks 56, 58) and the @magic/frame doubled-bilateral
# pattern (tick 27).
#
# Tick 59 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 58's residue:
# @smarts/magic landed at 219d095 (form/process-substrate altitude;
# second cross-family adapter). The family-root forward-promise set
# continues:
#
#   adapters: magic ✓  pack ✓  frame ← THIS  cyberpunk  epistemologic  kintsugi
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# @smarts.smarts records carry `frame_form: frame` as the second form
# field (per smarts.mirror tick 30 C4 closure). The typed-field
# already names the @frame identity at the @smarts integration
# altitude; this adapter EMPIRICALLY DISCHARGES the composition by
# exposing the bilateral predicate consumer species can name in
# `requires` clauses.
#
# Per the @magic/frame precedent (tick 27): the @frame altitude's
# bounded_commutator_check predicate takes (operator, frame,
# perturbation) at the typed boundary. This adapter's bilateral
# threads the operator as an explicit typed parameter — the operator
# does not live in the @smarts integration's typed fields; consumer
# species name it at the bilateral signature per [[feedback-no-bare-
# types]].
#
# === The adapter pattern (per @smarts/pack + @smarts/magic templates) ===
#
# @frame's family-root carriers (per shards/frame.mirror tick 23
# Seam consolidation):
#   - frame         gauge-visible cognitive position
#   - operator      typed locus the cognitive_order measures
#   - morphism      action whose commutator with D_F is probed
#   - commutator    bracketed [D_F, a] Tomm-probe pair
#   - perturbation  what bounded_commutator_check applies
#
# @smarts's family-root carriers (per shards/smarts.mirror #83):
#   - smarts        record {magic_form, frame_form: frame, ...}
#   - deployment    record {form, host, manifest}
#
# The substrate-pull-correct mapping (already typed at @smarts
# carrier altitude; this adapter exposes the bilateral):
#
#   smarts.frame_form  ↔ frame  (field-projection; the load-bearing
#                                  identity)
#   smarts             ↔ frame-extended-with-integration
#
# === The doubled-bilateral structural shape ===
#
# Per @magic/frame template: the bilateral predicate discharges TWO
# family predicates in one clause:
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p) (@smarts family-root): the substrate-
#      architectural-integration discipline verifier per #83.
#
#   2. bounded_commutator_check(op, frame_form_of(s), p) (@frame
#      family-root): the cognitive-order discipline verifier per #82.
#      Discharges that the operator's substrate-architectural support
#      for the frame (recovered from the @smarts integration's
#      frame_form field) survives perturbation with bounded
#      commutator. FLEXIBLE → bounded; DEFENSIVE → unbounded.
#
# Both must hold for the smarts integration to satisfy @frame at
# cognitive-order altitude.
#
# === Why `smarts_satisfies_frame` takes operator as explicit param ===
#
# Per @magic/frame tick 27 + [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: the @frame
# bilateral's operator parameter is NOT in the @smarts integration's
# typed fields. The signature takes operator explicitly so the
# consumer species names the typed operator at the requires clause
# boundary; the substrate-decl is structurally honest about the
# parameter that doesn't reduce to a field projection.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern (GoF)       Gamma-Helm-Johnson-Vlissides 1994.
#                               Inherited via @smarts/{pack, magic}.
#   functor adjunction          Mac Lane 1971. The mathematical
#                               ancestor of cross-family composition.
#   Bateson logical type        Bateson 1972; 1964. Grounds why
#                               cognitive-altitude (@frame) and
#                               integration-altitude (@smarts) need
#                               an adapter rather than collapse.
#   Tomm reflexive questions    Tomm 1988. @frame's substrate-
#                               mathematical primitive; threaded into
#                               @smarts integration via this adapter.
#   knowledge commons           Ostrom 1990. The hosting-discipline
#                               ancestor of @smarts integration.
#
# === What this adapter does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Does NOT make every frame automatically a @smarts integration.
# 2. Does NOT absorb @frame into @smarts.
# 3. Does NOT discharge per-altitude @frame species shards' (pre/in/
#    of/on/across) bilateral discipline at the @smarts integration
#    altitude; the @pack peers consume those altitudes directly per
#    the @frame altitude partition (tick 57 C4 deferred work).
# 4. Does NOT supersede @magic/frame's cognitive-altitude bridge
#    — @magic/frame bridges @magic (form-side at substrate altitude)
#    with @frame; @smarts/frame bridges @smarts (form-side at
#    deployment altitude) with @frame. Different altitudes; both
#    valid; orthogonal.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at cognitive-order-altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole adapter (honest): smarts_satisfies_frame returns
# SATISFIED only when BOTH bilaterals discharge substantively. The
# @smarts discipline_flexible AND the @frame bounded_commutator_check
# both hold under perturbation; the @smarts integration's frame_form
# represents what the operator substantively-supports cognitively.
#
# Narcissus-pole adapter (deceptive): smarts_satisfies_frame returns
# SATISFIED via vocabulary-only verification. The @smarts integration
# claims frame discipline via name-only (the frame_form field is
# populated but the operator's substrate-architectural support
# diverges from the claimed cognitive_order).
#
# Per the @magic/frame + @smarts/{pack, magic} precedent + #57: the
# adapter MUST NOT permit Narcissus-pole bypass. The bilateral's two
# `requires` clauses discharge to BOTH family predicates;
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) at @io enforces the
# discrimination.
#
# Spec context: shards/smarts.mirror (the @smarts family-root);
#               shards/frame.mirror (the @frame family-root).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]],
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-test]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Related shards: smarts.mirror, frame.mirror, magic/frame.mirror
#                 (cognitive-altitude adapter precedent at substrate
#                 altitude; orthogonal),
#                 smarts/pack.mirror, smarts/magic.mirror (sibling
#                 cross-family adapters in the @smarts forward-promise
#                 set).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/smarts/frame.mirror`
# declares `@smarts/frame` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/mathematics/mac-lane-1971
source @arxiv/cybernetics/bateson-1972
source @arxiv/therapy/tomm-1988
source @arxiv/common-goods/ostrom-1990

# === frame_form_of adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action projecting the @frame
# instance from a @smarts integration. The smarts.frame_form field
# IS the @frame at the substrate-decl altitude; this projection
# EXPOSES the field as a substrate-decl operation the bilateral
# predicate can name.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
frame_form_of(s: smarts) -> frame { \ }

# === frame_as_smarts adapter ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a @frame instance
# to a @smarts integration with the frame_form field populated. Other
# smarts fields populated as default refs at the lift altitude;
# consumer species needing other fields use the other
# @smarts/<family> adapters.
#
# Round-trip identity at the frame_form altitude:
#   frame_form_of(frame_as_smarts(f)) = f
# for all frame f. Cheapest falsification check.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
frame_as_smarts(f: frame) -> smarts { \ }

# === smarts_satisfies_frame bilateral predicate ===
#
# THE CROSS-FAMILY BILATERAL PREDICATE in @smarts that discharges
# BOTH parent-family AND child-family verdicts in one clause. The
# substrate-pull-correct way to mechanically discharge the cognitive-
# order-altitude composition claim that the @smarts family-root
# preserved as forward-promised at #83.
#
# Three `requires` clauses (two are load-bearing the doubled-
# bilateral; the third is implicit via the @frame bilateral's own
# discipline):
#
#   1. discipline_flexible(s, p)
#      — the @smarts family-root predicate.
#
#   2. bounded_commutator_check(op, frame_form_of(s), p)
#      — the @frame family-root predicate. Discharges that the
#      operator's substrate-architectural support for the
#      @smarts-integrated frame survives perturbation with bounded
#      commutator.
#
# Both must hold for the smarts integration to satisfy @frame at
# cognitive-order altitude. The cross-family composition mechanically
# discharges the cognitive-order identity claim the frame_form: frame
# typed-field carries at @smarts integration altitude.
#
# The signature takes smarts, operator, and perturbation as explicit
# typed parameters per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] because the operator
# does not live in the @smarts integration's typed fields and the
# consumer species names it at the typed boundary.
#
# Consumer species (forward-promised @smarts species shards
# implementing the four Models; @pack peers consuming @frame altitudes
# substantively; @spectral/garden/smarts hosted deployment) name this
# predicate when their operation requires cross-family discharge.
smarts_satisfies_frame(s: smarts, op: operator, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires discipline_flexible(s, p)
requires bounded_commutator_check(op, frame_form_of(s), p)
{ \ }

# === Honest hedge per @magic/frame + @smarts/{pack, magic} precedent ===
#
# This adapter closes the frame_form-projection altitude of
# "@smarts integrates @frame at substrate altitude":
#  - frame ↔ smarts.frame_form round-trips via frame_as_smarts /
#    frame_form_of.
#  - The bilateral smarts_satisfies_frame discharges BOTH family
#    predicates simultaneously.
#
# It does NOT close round-trip identity at the smarts-as-whole
# altitude (other @smarts/<family> adapters cover other fields).
#
# Honest claim post-adapter:
#  - "@smarts integrates @frame at frame_form altitude" — CLOSED.
#  - "@smarts integrates @frame at smarts-as-whole altitude" —
#    FORWARD-PROMISED pending the full cross-family adapter set.

out @smarts/frame
out frame_form_of
out frame_as_smarts
out smarts_satisfies_frame
